%% POST /orders as implemented in order.controller.ts and create-order.use-case.ts.
%% Isolation (READ COMMITTED), lock_timeout and statement_timeout are set once per
%% connection in the pool's startup packet, not per transaction.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant Controller as OrderController<br/>(POST /orders)
    participant Idem as IdempotencyService
    participant UoW as UnitOfWork
    participant UseCase as CreateOrderUseCase
    participant Catalog as CatalogService
    participant Prices as PriceResolver<br/>(SqlPriceResolver)
    participant Orders as OrderRepository
    participant Moves as StockMovementService
    participant Reserv as ReservationRepository
    participant Outbox as OutboxRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Client->>Controller: POST /orders { warehouse_id, items[{product_id, quantity}] }<br/>optional Idempotency-Key header
    Note over Controller: Guards: rate limit, JWT, @Roles('buyer','buyer_admin')<br/>Body validated by createOrderRequestSchema (no price field)

    alt Idempotency-Key present (ADR 0015)
        Controller->>Idem: execute({orgId, endpoint, key, requestHash}, work)
        Idem->>DB: claim the key in its own committed statement
        Note over Idem: A completed key replays the stored response.<br/>An in-progress key or a different request hash is refused.
        Idem->>UoW: withTransaction(work)
    else no key
        Controller->>UoW: withTransaction(work)
    end
    UoW->>DB: BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL READ COMMITTED
    UoW->>UseCase: execute(tx, actor, input, now)

    Note over UseCase: 1. AUTHORISE
    UseCase->>UseCase: assertRole(actor, 'buyer', 'buyer_admin')<br/>actor.orgType must be 'buyer'<br/>normalise lines, reject empty or repeated products
    UseCase->>Catalog: findWarehouse(tx, warehouseId)
    Catalog->>DB: SELECT warehouse
    UseCase->>UseCase: 404 if missing, 409 if inactive

    Note over UseCase: 2. PRICE (two queries)
    UseCase->>Prices: resolve(tx, orgScopeOf(actor), {id, type: 'buyer'}, lines, now)
    Prices->>Catalog: findProducts(tx, ids)
    Catalog->>DB: SELECT products
    Prices->>DB: SELECT price_list_items JOIN price_lists<br/>WHERE product_id = ANY($1) AND (org_id = $2 OR org_id IS NULL)<br/>AND status = 'active' AND valid_from <= $3 AND (valid_to IS NULL OR valid_to > $3)
    Prices->>Prices: pickPrice() per line: contract before default,<br/>priority, largest tier ≤ qty, else base_price
    Prices-->>UseCase: priced lines

    Note over UseCase: 3. WRITE ORDER AND LINES
    UseCase->>Orders: insert(tx, {buyerOrgId, placedByUserId, warehouseId,<br/>subtotal, total, reservationExpiresAt = now + TTL})
    Orders->>DB: INSERT INTO orders (order_code from next_order_code())
    UseCase->>Orders: insertItems(tx, orderId, items sorted by SKU)
    Orders->>DB: INSERT INTO order_items (order_id, product_id, quantity,<br/>unit_price, line_total, price_list_item_id)

    Note over UseCase: 4. RESERVE, line by line in product-id order
    loop each item, sorted by product id
        UseCase->>Moves: reserve(tx, {productId, warehouseId, qty}, {orderId, reservationId, ...})
        Moves->>DB: UPDATE inventory SET available_qty = available_qty - $3,<br/>reserved_qty = reserved_qty + $3, version = version + 1<br/>WHERE product_id = $1 AND warehouse_id = $2 AND available_qty >= $3<br/>RETURNING ...
        alt row returned (row lock held until commit)
            Moves->>DB: INSERT INTO inventory_transactions<br/>(txn_type 'reserve', before/after quantities, order_id, reservation_id)
            Moves-->>UseCase: move
        else zero rows
            Moves-->>UseCase: null
            UseCase->>DB: read current level (for the error details)
            UseCase-->>UoW: throw INSUFFICIENT_STOCK {product_id, sku, requested, available}
            UoW->>DB: ROLLBACK (undoes the order, lines and every earlier reservation)
            Note over Idem: With a key: the key is released (marked failed)<br/>after the rollback, so the client may retry with it
            Controller-->>Client: 409 { error: { code: 'INSUFFICIENT_STOCK', details } }<br/>details.available reveals the stock level (open question, ADR 0013)
        end
    end

    Note over UseCase: 5. RECORD
    UseCase->>Reserv: insertMany(tx, held)
    Reserv->>DB: INSERT INTO inventory_reservations (status defaults to 'held')<br/>(fk_itx_reservation is deferred, checked at commit)
    UseCase->>Outbox: append(tx, order.created, orgId = buyer org)
    Outbox->>DB: INSERT INTO outbox_events (aggregate_type, aggregate_id, event_type, org_id, payload)

    UseCase-->>UoW: order with items
    UoW->>DB: COMMIT
    Note over DB: One commit: order, order_items, inventory rows,<br/>ledger rows, reservations, outbox event
    Note over Idem: With a key: the key was marked completed (response stored)<br/>inside this same transaction, just before COMMIT
    Controller-->>Client: 201 { data: order }
